From e938c6e543d846de483d8de09bf7a6ecccd1bda2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:06:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] desktop: reconnect retires turnLive-only claims;
 only needs-input rows track prompt inputs

PR #1892 review nits (t_01a1d36ee96f8481):

- reconcileBusyStatesOnReconnect skipped a state with turnLive but no
  busy/awaitingResponse claim (after Stop, before the terminal event).
  Since #1892 supersededPromptRuntimes leaves a turn-live sibling alone,
  so a backend restart in that window kept its dead prompt, and the red
  stripe, forever. Reconnect now downgrades turnLive-only claims too
  (store mirror and the tile delegate's retireBusyClaim), so the new
  runtime's turn retires the prompt as usual.
- useSessionRowStripe subscribed every sidebar row to
  $stuckPromptInputsKey, re-rendering them all whenever any runtime's
  prompt set changed. Only needs-input rows read it; other rows now
  subscribe to a constant atom. The re-report-on-move test still holds.
---
